  "live_records": {
    "q-73747": {
      "dom_id": "step-q73747",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$, given the points $A(-1,1,1)$, $B(2,-2,1)$, $C(1,2,2)$, and $D(2,-1,4).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(2i-2j+k)-(-i+j+k) \\\\  & =3i-3j \\\\  & =⟨3,-3,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i+2j+2k)-(-i+j+k) \\\\  & =2i+j+k \\\\  & =⟨2,1,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(2i-j+4k)-(-i+j+k) \\\\  & =3i-2j+3k \\\\  & =⟨3,-2,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|-(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(1\\cdot 3-(-2)\\cdot 1)+3(2\\cdot 3-3\\cdot 1)+0 \\\\  & =15+9 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|24|=24.\n$$",
